            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-44160",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Fluentd is Vulnerable to Denial of Service (DoS) via Gzip Decompression Bomb in `in_http` and `in_forward`"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Fluentd collects events from various data sources and writes them to files, RDBMS, NoSQL, IaaS, SaaS, Hadoop and so on. Prior to 1.19.3, Fluentd's in_http and in_forward plugins support gzip-compressed data but enforce limits only on compressed payloads through settings such as body_size_limit and chunk_size_limit, allowing crafted compressed payloads to decompress in memory to an excessive size and cause denial of service through memory exhaustion. This issue is fixed in version 1.19.3."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44160",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-44160\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: fluentd\nFixed Version: \u003e= 1.19.3\nLink: [CVE-2026-44160](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44160)\nFluentd collects events from various data sources and writes them to files, RDBMS, NoSQL, IaaS, SaaS, Hadoop and so on. Prior to 1.19.3, Fluentd's in_http and in_forward plugins support gzip-compressed data but enforce limits only on compressed payloads through settings such as body_size_limit and chunk_size_limit, allowing crafted compressed payloads to decompress in memory to an excessive size and cause denial of service through memory exhaustion. This issue is fixed in version 1.19.3.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-44160**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|fluentd|\u003e= 1.19.3|[CVE-2026-44160](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44160)|\n\nFluentd collects events from various data sources and writes them to files, RDBMS, NoSQL, IaaS, SaaS, Hadoop and so on. Prior to 1.19.3, Fluentd's in_http and in_forward plugins support gzip-compressed data but enforce limits only on compressed payloads through settings such as body_size_limit and chunk_size_limit, allowing crafted compressed payloads to decompress in memory to an excessive size and cause denial of service through memory exhaustion. This issue is fixed in version 1.19.3."
